{
  "_comment": [
    "Every CALLS, REFERENCES, IMPORTS, EXTENDS and IMPLEMENTS relationship in",
    "the fixture, read from the source by hand. All five are closed.",
    "",
    "The rules the entries follow (docs/benchmark.md, 'Code relationships'):",
    "",
    "- The source of a code edge is the innermost function, method, class or",
    "  interface the occurrence sits in. Module-level code, including the",
    "  initialiser of a module-level variable, belongs to the file.",
    "- CALLS is an invocation: f(), ns.f(), obj.m(), and new C() when C declares",
    "  a constructor. super() of a class with no declared constructor calls",
    "  nothing the graph can name.",
    "- REFERENCES is any other use of a declared name, heritage clauses included.",
    "- Names in import and export specifiers are neither: they only make the",
    "  file depend on another file.",
    "- IMPORTS joins two files when one has an import or re-export from the other,",
    "  or refers to something declared in it (the documented contract).",
    "- EXTENDS targets a class. IMPLEMENTS targets an interface or a member: a type",
    "  implements every interface it satisfies through its heritage, directly or",
    "  through a base class or interface, and a member implements every supertype",
    "  member it implements or overrides. An interface extending an interface is",
    "  IMPLEMENTS in this model.",
    "- External symbols (value.toFixed) are not in the graph and have no edges.",
    "",
    "Revision note: the first draft of this file listed only the nearest",
    "supertype for IMPLEMENTS. That was wrong as a statement of fact (Square does",
    "implement Shape) and the documented model does not say 'direct only', so",
    "the transitive edges were added. Everything else is as first written.",
    "",
    "`knownGap` and `knownFalsePositives` record defects confirmed against the raw",
    "SCIP index. They are scored (recall and precision include them); they do not",
    "fail the run, and a gap that disappears does fail it until it is removed here."
  ],
